 see how  that this is possible in the offline  setting because you can cheat because  you can treat each element label pair as  a parallel copy of the element but it  turns out this is highly non-trivial  online and we  show that nevertheless you can do it um  in the random order model um and then  and this is where a lot of the technical  work in the paper goes  and for more detail i refer you to the  paper and the longer talk  so this is the picture we end up with  and we conclude that all these four  problems are equivalent up to constant  factors  so to conclude uh i showed that the  matrix secondary problem is equivalent  to online contention resolution in the  random order model for these  uncontentious distributions and this is  interesting because um  the contention resolution problem we get  is obviously stochastic in nature and  ordinal in nature  um now the contention resolution problem  we reduce to  is challenging because it features  positive correlation in the input set  however this positive correlation is not  arbitrary it seems somewhat benign in  particular in my original paper i have a  polyhedral characterization of  uncontentious distributions and  hopefully if we can use this  characterization to help in online  contention resolution then that might  help resolve the matrix secretary  conjecture  and that's all i have thanks  thanks very much uh i think i think  there might be a quick  [Music]  or not but i i think i think we'll uh  conclude there we're just about exactly  on top so  well thank thanks very much that's the  end of this session  you
 

